@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-credentials-are-native-and-confined
The native adapter MUST keep Pully sessions and optional Access credentials in this
app's non-synchronizing Keychain, accessible only while unlocked on this device.
Credential records MUST be bound to the normalized configured server and account,
MUST NOT be returned for another server, and MUST NOT enter URLs, defaults, logs or
analytics. Native code MUST NOT implement a second Pully RPC client. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision, the chosen plan's Authentication section,
and root phone-api-one-account and google-sign-in-same-account.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] ios-account-reset-invalidates-observers
Sign-out, server changes and credential changes MUST synchronously invalidate the
active source before another source can be used. A late sign-in or verification
answer for an earlier source MUST NOT install credentials. A restored Keychain
session MUST require server verification before it becomes the active account.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 iOS decision and chosen account/cache ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] ios-google-uses-registered-native-client
Native Google sign-in MUST remain unavailable without a registered iOS client and
its reversed-client-ID callback scheme. It MUST request an ID token for the
existing server's web client ID, and MUST leave signature, audience, expiry and
email-allowlist validation to that server. The Google adapter MUST NOT add GitHub
OAuth or store a Google client secret. The separately owned public personal-account
flow MUST NOT reuse Google or legacy account authority. Source: root
google-sign-in-same-account, Tavi's separate personal GitHub request and the chosen
21 Oct 2026 iOS plan's Authentication section.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] ios-model-choice-preserves-the-private-source
A model/engine preference change MUST retain the configured server, Access credentials,
verified session and source generation. A request from an older source generation MUST
NOT update the current model preferences. The real native preferences MUST keep the
choice for the next launch, without another RPC client or credential store. Source:
settings-model-row-names-the-model, client-invalidates-old-sources and Tavi's 21 Oct
2026 maximum-reuse iOS settings decision, preserving Android ServerStore.save behavior.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-incoming-envelopes-feed-the-shared-owner
Native URL delivery MUST accept only bounded credential-free HTTPS links to GitHub
or the configured server origin, either directly or inside the single explicit
pully://open?url= envelope. It MUST preserve the destination's path, query and fragment
for the shared parser, never reconfigure a server or implement another route stack.
Google callbacks MUST be consumed before ordinary links in the same batch; a closed
scene receiver MUST be inert. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS native link plan,
including cold/warm delivery, auth priority and source isolation.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-share-source-revocation-precedes-publication
The optional identity-replacement hook MUST run synchronously before publishing a
different endpoint, Access policy or account, and before sign-out or credential
reset publishes an anonymous source. Same-account session renewal, successful
restored verification, retries and scene recreation MUST NOT rotate a share source
token. Handoff storage failure MUST fail closed for imports without blocking ordinary
credential cleanup. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 native share handoff plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] ios-personal-blob-has-separate-private-storage
The personal Pully session vault MUST use a separate app-private, nonsynchronizing
Keychain item accessible only while unlocked on this device. The native adapter
MUST atomically replace the complete bounded blob, preserve its previous contents
on failure, and reject empty or oversized data without deleting another credential.
Only an absent item MAY become a successful missing read; locked, unavailable or
corrupt storage MUST fail. It MUST NOT use UserDefaults, plaintext, a shared access
group or the legacy account's credential service. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026
personal GitHub request and accepted 22 Oct native secure-stage/confirm/publish plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-personal-active-events-are-synchronous
The personal-account activity adapter MUST synchronously report the actual scene's
active state on registration and every active/inactive transition. Cancellation
MUST detach exactly its registration. Reentrant inactivity or disconnection MUST
prevent an obsolete active event, and a closed adapter MUST remain inactive. The
existing Home started/background event meanings MUST remain unchanged. Source:
the accepted 22 Oct native personal lifecycle plan and independent mounted sign-in
foreground-race finding.
